{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/372","id":4719395650,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABGUxDQg","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/372","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/372.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/372.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/372","number":372,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"9700034: reviewed SIRSN maximal-route criteria; original unsolved 5/5","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Disposition\nOriginal **unsolved, 5/5 substantive author turns**. The expected maximum over iid uniform sampled destinations is not proved finite from ordinary SIRSN axioms, and no genuine SIRSN counterexample is claimed.\n\nThe full five-turn packet proves:\n1. A credited uniform corollary of Kahn’s Poisson-road estimates, giving all maximal-length moments q<gamma−1\n2. A countably sampled FDD increment criterion, with an explicit extra route-length triangle/moment sufficient condition\n3. Tail-visibility and two-route criteria that distinguish positive endpoint mass from its mean\n4. Unconditional finite exterior-arc union and confinement almost surely, integrable fixed-root portions, and localization of the remaining maximal estimates\n5. A genuine countable-mixture reduction and a proof that fixed-base affine anisotropy cannot produce the required counterexample family\n\nAll extra hypotheses remain explicit. Almost-sure finiteness of finitely many exterior arcs does **not** establish their expected length. Scalar critical fields and random-environment examples are diagnostic only and have no SIRSN realization. Known Kahn and Aldous inputs and classical methods are credited; historical novelty is unverified.\n\n## Source and review\nThe target is Aldous’s 2012 Problem34, renumbered Problem8 in the 2014 paper. It concerns Euclidean arclength and a countable sampled maximum; travel time, route-length triangle inequalities and continuum versions cannot be substituted silently.\n\n- [Current reviewed status](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/f30fb696da92fd4b998d61859d6ed06012ce78d4/problems/9700034_sirsn_maximal_routes/REVIEWED_STATUS.md)\n- [Full result and exact gap](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/f30fb696da92fd4b998d61859d6ed06012ce78d4/problems/9700034_sirsn_maximal_routes/FINAL_RESULT.md)\n- [Primary source map](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/f30fb696da92fd4b998d61859d6ed06012ce78d4/problems/9700034_sirsn_maximal_routes/FINAL_SOURCE_MAP.md)\n- [Independent full source/proof review](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/f30fb696da92fd4b998d61859d6ed06012ce78d4/problems/9700034_sirsn_maximal_routes/review/REVIEW.md)\n\nIndependent AI-assisted review: PASS for all scoped claims, no mandatory revision. All **503,419** author assertions replay exactly; **2,507** separate controls pass. The audit checked 64 public bindings and four primary files. Finite controls supplement the continuum proofs and do not formally certify the model or the unresolved universal claim.\n\nRun `python verify_publication.py` with standard Python, optionally `--source-dir` for separately obtained source files. Raw sources, imported records, images and the unbound working audit are excluded.\n\n## Preservation and scope\nAll **38 frozen author files and six manifest-bound review files** are preserved byte-for-byte. Four additive publication wrappers provide current status and portable verification. All 48 remote artifact contents and raw Git blobs match exactly. The only non-target change is rank397’s QUEUE status/turn cells, queued0/5 → unsolved5/5.\n\nFresh main `efd29c05204703acca9a0860812f54b94fae54b1` is the first parent; final author WIP `6f29bc5129f519ef5d6cb8901f5abb35868c4d03` is preserved as second parent. One draft PR for this target; no merge or release requested.","created_at":"2026-10-02T17:25:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T17:25:43Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"f13ff4d7cdeec27842644bda72c8d975ee4c833d","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/372/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/372/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/372/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/f30fb696da92fd4b998d61859d6ed06012ce78d4","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:math/9700034-sirsn-maximal-routes-reviewed","ref":"math/9700034-sirsn-maximal-routes-reviewed","sha":"f30fb696da92fd4b998d61859d6ed06012ce78d4","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"h